0..75 Comment "// A Tarski universe closed under pairs and paths, with its decoder arms in"
76..99 Comment "// their intended form."
100..102 Comment "//"
103..181 Comment "// Martin-Löf\'s universe is closed under dependent functions, dependent pairs"
182..257 Comment "// and identity types. Each such code decodes to a family at the decodes of"
258..317 Comment "// its fields. A decode thus stands as a family\'s argument."
318..320 Comment "//"
321..396 Comment "// Each code is its own block. One refusal thus leaves the others standing."
397..471 Comment "// The front end refuses a pair of decodes as calls. The checker refuses a"
472..545 Comment "// dependent pair\'s second family at the first decode. The fragment check"
546..617 Comment "// refuses a path\'s carrier as a marked call by its sort. A run binds a"
618..690 Comment "// decode as a type of its own. A field at the code\'s decode then stands"
691..708 Comment "// apart from it."
709..711 Comment "//"
712..778 Comment "// - see: #3572 — not implemented: a call as a family\'s argument"
779..859 Comment "// - see: #3571 — not implemented: the second family at the first one\'s quoted"
860..871 Comment "//   decode"
872..946 Comment "// - see: #3681 — a marked call as a path\'s carrier, refused by its sort"
947..1017 Comment "// - see: `model/universe/inductive-recursive.gandr` — the dependent"
1018..1042 Comment "//   functions, admitted"
1043..1113 Comment "// - see: Martin-Löf, _Intuitionistic Type Theory_, Bibliopolis, 1984"
1115..1131 Comment "// The naturals."
